{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And Pharaoh awoke, and behold, a dream.</b> It should have said 'and behold, dreams' (והנה חלומות), for there were two dreams — the dream of the cows and the dream of the stalks. But it says 'a dream' (חלום), because he himself recognized that the two were one matter, only he did not know their interpretation."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:19:09.543936466Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}